  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Rafael. You're verified, and I'm sorry the team lunch came up short.\n\nI checked order K-6201 from Taqueria Luz. It was delivered at 12:24 PM today, so you're well within the 48-hour window for reporting missing items. Here's what you're owed for the missing food:\n\n- **2 carne asada tacos** (2 \u00d7 $4.50 = $9.00)\n- **1 veggie burrito** ($12.00)\n\nYou can choose how to get each item back:\n\n**Option A: Refund to your card (Visa ending 4242)**\nYour order used the promo code OFFICE16, which took 10% off. So part of each item's price was never charged to your card. That part comes back as Forkful credit, and the rest goes to your card:\n- Tacos: $8.10 to card + $0.90 credit\n- Burrito: $10.80 to card + $1.20 credit\n- **Total: $18.90 to your card + $2.10 in credit**\n\n**Option B: Forkful account credit (item price + 20%)**\n- Tacos: $10.80 credit\n- Burrito: $14.40 credit\n\nTogether that's $25.20, which is over the $25 limit on credit I can give in one conversation. So only one of the two items can be credit, and the other has to go back to your card as in Option A. For example:\n- Tacos as $10.80 credit, and the burrito refunded as $10.80 to card + $1.20 credit, **or**\n- Burrito as $14.40 credit, and the tacos refunded as $8.10 to card + $0.90 credit\n\nSince this was paid with the company card, the card refund (Option A) may be easiest. Which would you like?\n\nAlso, the restaurant had run out of 2 of your 4 horchatas, and those were already refunded to your card automatically ($8.00). If you only got 2 horchatas, that's why."
  },
